'''Barista Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained by beating [[Fascinating Fallen Tower/Floor 10|Floor 10]] of the [[Fascinating Fallen Tower]]. It was added in [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 857
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Barista Cat
|name2 = Silver Nyanko Ranger
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Silver Nyanko Ranger''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Cat is an anti-[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] DPS with a very fast attack rate. Against Angels, it possesses a solid 6,500 DPS with a decently high standing range. This is good for countering Angels in the early-game, such as [[Angelic Gory]] and [[Boraphim]], especially when you don't have any better answers. However, it quickly loses steam as soon as you unlock [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], who tends to outclass it in terms of damage and spammability, while also having Area Attack to boot. While Silver Nyanko Ranger is tankier, its recharge rate is subpar even with [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Ranger]]'s [[Blue Strike (Combo)|Combo]], and it costs a lot to deploy even with [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]]'s [[Green Strike (Combo)|Combo]]. There's little reason to use Silver Nyanko Ranger outside of its speed, which can allow it to sneak into enemy blind spots like [[Ange Lackey]]. However, even in this regard, [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] is better overall unit for that job.

[[Gold Silver Strike (Combo)|Gold Silver Strike]] does see powerful synergy with [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]] against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies, where it allows the [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] to survive nasty [[Death Surge]]s. It gives Red Nyanko Ranger viability against enemies which would have instantly evaporated it with Surge Attacks like [[Medu-san]] and the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]]. It is situationally useful on [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Ranger]] for similar reasons, but keep in mind, the Combo does take up 2 slots, and Silver Nyanko Ranger won't be contributing much to those fights. This Combo also lets it become a soft-counter to [[St. Dober]] for strategies that involve brute-forcing him.

Silver Nyanko Ranger can still serve as additional DPS alongside the units that outclass it, but in most situations, their acquisition means its demotion to [[Underground Labyrinth]] fodder.

